        a                   crmsci:S4_Observation ;
        ecrm:P2_has_type    <http://data.silknow.org/observation/technical-observation> ;
        ecrm:P3_has_note    "Octagonal panel; white silk embroidered with festoons of ribbon bows, flower garlands and tassels, surrounding a pendant map of the \"Western, or New World\" (showing the Americas and Australia) worked in fine black silk against white, flanked with figures, the left depicting a woman with a bird-cage in her lap showing a cross to a child, the right depicting the 18th century concept of a Native American with a feathered headdress, bow, and leopardskin apron. Glazed and framed in an octagonal narrow wooden marquetry frame."@en ;
        crmsci:O8_observed  <http://data.silknow.org/object/8b83b6ae-2b5b-34ee-9f05-7ef82a68174e> .

